# AGENTS.md

How to work in {{app_name}} (`{{project-name}}`), a native GPUI desktop app for macOS and
Linux. This is the only agent guide; `CLAUDE.md` imports it.

## Shape

One crate: a library (the app) plus a thin binary. GPUI, gpui-component and the bundled
icons come from one crates.io dependency, `gpui-kit`: import GPUI as `gpui_kit::*` and
components as `gpui_kit::component::*`.

- `src/main.rs`: command line only. Unknown arguments exit 2.
- `src/lib.rs`: actions, shortcuts, menus, `run` and the main window.
- `src/launch.rs`: the `APP_*` environment variables, including the dry-run switch.
- `src/shell.rs`: the root view (page state, settings, title bar). The pages are `impl Shell`
  blocks in `home.rs` and `settings_view.rs`.
- `src/palette.rs`: the ⌘K command palette.
- `src/ui.rs`: `group` and `row` for settings-style layouts.
- `src/theme.rs`: 13 px type, greys, the accent. `src/settings.rs`: JSON preferences.
- `src/tray.rs` (`--features tray`), `src/login_item.rs` (macOS).
- `examples/shot.rs`: headless screenshots.

## The loop

- `cargo run` / `just run`. Build before you run: a stale `target/debug` binary doesn't know
  new flags (it exits 2 on them) or new code.
- `just ci` before calling anything done: fmt check, clippy `-D warnings` on default and
  `--all-features`, tests, and builds of both. Paste its output; never claim done while red.
- `just fix` applies clippy's machine fixes and formats.

## Seeing the UI without taking over the desktop

- **`just shot <home|settings> <light|dark> out.png`** renders the real views with the real
  renderer into a 2x PNG: no window, no Dock icon, no focus change, identical across runs.
  `APP_FIXTURES=1 just shot home dark out.png` shows sample data. It needs the GPU, so it
  fails inside sandboxes like macOS Seatbelt: run it outside, or ask the user to. It renders
  the view only (no traffic lights or window shadow).
- **`just dry-run`** (`APP_DRY_RUN=1 cargo run`) launches the real app without activating it,
  using `settings.dry-run.json`, with nothing irreversible (no login-item changes).
  `APP_PAGE=settings` and `APP_APPEARANCE=dark` start it in a given state.
- Never drive the app with global keystrokes or UI scripting: they land in whatever app is
  frontmost. To reach a state, add an `APP_*` variable in `src/launch.rs`. To check an
  interaction, write a test with `gpui_kit::test` (see the tests in `src/shell.rs`).

## Definition of done

1. `just ci` is green.
2. UI changes: `just shot` in light and dark, and you looked at both images.
3. No new or changed dependencies unless the user approved them.

## Code

- Comments explain a non-obvious why: a gotcha, a constraint, a choice that looks wrong.
  Don't restate the code or narrate history; git has the history.
- Docs describe what exists now. Delete a sentence when it stops being true.
- No `todo!()` or `dbg!()`. Never ignore a `Result` (`unused_must_use` is denied).
- `unsafe_code` is denied; a necessary exception needs a scoped allow and a `// SAFETY:` comment.
- `.expect()` is fine for genuinely infallible GPUI calls; prefer `?` elsewhere.
- Shortcuts go in `shortcuts()` (`src/lib.rs`), bound with `KeyBinding::load`:
  `KeyBinding::new` panics at launch on `secondary-`. A test parses every shortcut.
- A command is one action with a menu item, an optional shortcut and a palette row
  (`src/palette.rs`), so all three run one handler and the row shows the shortcut.
- Tray menu handlers call functions (`show_main_window`), not actions: with no focused window
  an action reaches nothing.

## Look and feel

- Body text is `text_base` (13 px), secondary text `text_sm`. Nothing smaller in your own views.
- Build from components (`TitleBar`, `TabBar::segmented`, `GroupBox` via `ui::group`,
  `Switch`, `Select`, `Empty`, `Alert`, `Dialog`, `Form`/`field`, `Command`), not hand-drawn
  look-alikes.
- Gotchas: tabs in the title bar need a `prevent_default` mouse-down wrapper or clicking them
  drags the window; the segmented indicator is drawn in `background`, so the track
  (`tab_bar_segmented`) is darker in dark mode; `Field` descriptions default to `text_xs`;
  gpui-component's `setting` renderers are crate-private (hence `ui.rs`); the palette renders
  inside `Shell`, not in a `Dialog`, or its rows' actions never reach Shell's handlers.

## Performance

The UI thread never waits on the network or a large file: run that on
`cx.background_executor()` and `cx.notify()` when it's done. A small write at a coarse
boundary (a click, a blur) can stay synchronous, as the settings do; never write per keystroke.
Notify the smallest entity that changed and render long lists with `uniform_list`. More in
`docs/LEARNINGS.md` and `docs/background-jobs.md`.

## Upgrading GPUI

1. Bump `gpui-kit` in `Cargo.toml`. If the new release needs a newer Rust, bump
   `rust-version` there and `channel` in `rust-toolchain.toml` together.
2. `cargo update -p gpui-kit`
3. `just ci`
4. `just run` and `just shot`: some breakage only shows at runtime.
5. `cargo deny --all-features check licenses`

## Shipping

`just bundle` builds the `.app`; `just install` signs it ad hoc and replaces the copy in
`/Applications`. macOS notifications need the app launched from a bundle; "Open at login"
needs the installed copy.
